review-fixes.lust:5:7  Math is a C# type, not a value. Use what it has: Math:Something(…) or Math.Something
review-fixes.lust:6:25  Math is a C# type, not a value. Use what it has: Math:Something(…) or Math.Something
review-fixes.lust:6:33  Math is a C# type, not a value. Use what it has: Math:Something(…) or Math.Something
review-fixes.lust:7:5  Math is a C# type fetched in this file, so a variable can't use that name.
review-fixes.lust:9:1  h holds s, which is only declared further down, on line 10. Save and load after the variables are declared.
review-fixes.lust:11:15  Int32:TryParse uses C# features Lust can't use yet (out or ref parameters, generics, or values Lust has no type for).
review-fixes.lust:12:11  Parse belongs to C#'s Int64 type itself. Fetch it first with fetch cs:System.Int64; then use Int64:Parse(…)
review-fixes.lust:13:28  d is a DateTime (from C#), but this is nothing. A DateTime can't be nothing. Start it with new DateTime(…).
review-fixes.lust:14:14  give f a starting value, like do int(int) f = greet;
review-fixes.lust:16:11  jobs can't be saved: jobs's column f2 is a function, and functions belong to the program, not to a save.
review-fixes.lust:18:13  Length is a property, so it's read with a dot: q.Length
review-fixes.lust:19:16  a map's items are a key and a value, like ["apple" 3, "seed" 1].
review-fixes.lust:19:20  - works on numbers, but this has a string.
